  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 342 PM CST Sat Nov 14 2026\n\n...Synopsis...\n\nAmplified H5 ridging continues today into Sunday across the central \nCONUS, with troughing to the east and west of the area. This pattern \nwill slowly fill through the course of next week, giving way to \nsouthwest flow by Wednesday. Dry and very mild weather will be the \nresult, with 40s and 50s for highs on Sunday, then widespread 50s on \nMonday and Tuesday. \n\nRain chances return on Wednesday as a trough traverses the flow, \nwith ensembles still struggling to agree on the timing and intensity \nof the shortwave. Currently, precipitation looks to remain rather \nlight, and mainly north of Highway 200. Cooler air settles into the \narea late Wednesday into Thursday; however, with cold air situated \nwell north of the area, temperatures are expected to remain on the \nwarm side of average to slightly above average for mid November.",
